WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.499
Turn a problem into a hypothesis.

00:00:02.499 --> 00:00:08.745
Describe an observable learner problem and the behavior that would change if a solution worked.

00:00:08.745 --> 00:00:11.244
Learners lose their place between sessions.

00:00:11.244 --> 00:00:14.576
Offer a direct return to the last lesson.

00:00:14.576 --> 00:00:17.491
Measure resumed sessions that reach a lesson.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:19.802
Prioritize an opportunity.

00:00:19.802 --> 00:00:25.209
Compare opportunities using evidence, potential impact, and delivery effort.

00:00:25.209 --> 00:00:28.814
Record your assumptions alongside the decision.

00:00:28.814 --> 00:00:31.817
Collect repeated observations from learners.

00:00:31.817 --> 00:00:35.422
Estimate how many learners are affected.

00:00:35.422 --> 00:00:38.426
Identify dependencies and delivery costs.

00:00:38.917 --> 00:00:40.768
Design a learning experiment.

00:00:40.768 --> 00:00:45.860
Decide what evidence would support a decision before running an experiment.

00:00:45.860 --> 00:00:49.563
Choose one main measure and a useful guardrail.

00:00:49.563 --> 00:00:51.877
Track the intended behavioral outcome.

00:00:51.877 --> 00:00:55.117
Monitor a related cost or failure rate.

00:00:55.117 --> 00:00:58.357
Define when to adopt, revise, or stop.

